From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msi: Keep Level-zero features disabled through costing.

AI-assisted (Codex), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted
upstream.

Windows v14 disabled required children remain Request unknown and are not
published, including controls. Do not replace a child's zero Level with an
unselected parent's Level or copy a parent's state to it. E's worklist also
preserves disabled nodes. Shared v14 PDisabled/TDisabled checks, RULE_DISABLED.

Design MSI has no static Level0 feature. Its AddIns condition becomes Level0
for SWPersonalEdition=1, so this boundary can affect Personal Edition. Premium
clean-g5 is not modified. Condition-driven coverage remains a separate limit.

--- a/dlls/msi/action.c
+++ b/dlls/msi/action.c
@@ -1659,7 +1659,7 @@
 
     LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY( fl, &feature->Children, FeatureList, entry )
     {
-        if (!is_feature_selected( feature, level ) &&
+        if (fl->feature->Level > 0 && !is_feature_selected( feature, level ) &&
             feature->ActionRequest != INSTALLSTATE_LOCAL && feature->ActionRequest != INSTALLSTATE_SOURCE &&
             feature->ActionRequest != INSTALLSTATE_ADVERTISED)
         {
@@ -1681,7 +1681,7 @@
 
     LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY( fl, &feature->Children, FeatureList, entry )
     {
-        if ((fl->feature->Attributes & msidbFeatureAttributesFollowParent) &&
+        if (fl->feature->Level > 0 && (fl->feature->Attributes & msidbFeatureAttributesFollowParent) &&
             (!limit_level || is_feature_selected( fl->feature, level )))
         {
             TRACE("child %s (level %d request %d) follows parent %s (level %d request %d)\n",
